==English==

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|nl|oproer}} or {{der|en|de|Aufruhr}}<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>. Possibly influenced by ''[[roar]].''

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈʌpɹɔː/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈʌpɹɔːɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-uproar.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[tumultuous|Tumultuous]], [[noisy]] [[excitement]]. {{defdate|from 1520s}}
# [[loud|Loud]], [[confused]] [[noise]], especially when coming from several [[source]]s.
# A loud [[protest]], [[controversy]], or [[outrage]].

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:commotion]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|uproarious}}
* {{l|en|uproarish}}

